<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Template for the bump-proposer LaunchAgent (ADR-0028). Install with
     scripts/install-bump-proposer-launchd.sh, which substitutes __REPO_ROOT__ and __HOME__ and
     writes ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.devon.bump-proposer.plist.

     No secrets live here: the wrapper fetches the propose-scoped change-manager bearer from BWS
     at runtime under the broad machine account, and falls back to `gh auth token` for GitHub.

     THIS JOB WRITES, AND IT WRITES MORE THAN ITS SIBLINGS DO. It passes --submit, so a pass
     edits two lines of a standing package in the intent-packages checkout, takes the revision
     through that repository's audited lifecycle, approves it by conformance to
     approval-policy.toml, re-pins the hash fixture, COMMITS those three files, and proposes a
     work record in change-manager. The bare command is a dry run and the wrapper refuses to
     supply --submit itself, so the flag lives here where an operator reads it -- the same
     arrangement work-carrier's --register and change-proposer's --submit already use.

     THE HUMAN GATE DOES NOT MOVE. ADR-0028 keeps it at record approval, downstream of the mint,
     and the bearer this job holds is propose-scoped: it cannot approve the record it writes.
     change-manager refuses every status-moving route for that scope whatever the client sends.

     06:50, AND THE SLOT BUYS LESS THAN THE WRAPPER'S HEADER CLAIMS. Daily rather than hourly
     is the wrapper's argument and it holds: every writing pass commits to a checkout on this
     machine, so a pass that proposes something is a commit somebody has to notice. What does
     NOT hold is the same-day-carry clause. The carry is a single daily firing at 07:05 and it
     reads only APPROVED records; a record this job proposes is pending, so it is carried the
     same day only if a person approves it inside a fifteen-minute window, and otherwise waits
     for 07:05 tomorrow whatever hour this job runs. 06:50 is chosen because it is daily, it is
     early, and it leaves the existing slots intact -- 07:05 carry, 07:10 sweep, 07:30 ledger.
     Moving it later would cost nothing a reader should expect it to cost.

     THE PASS COMMITS ON THE CHECKOUT'S CURRENT BRANCH AND NEVER PUSHES. That is the producer's
     existing behaviour, kept rather than changed, and it is the whole design content of this
     increment: `standing.commit` says the branch is somebody else's to move. So a pass that
     proposes work leaves `~/Projects/intent-packages` one commit ahead of its upstream, which
     the activation sweep records in every row as `ahead_by` and deliberately does not classify.
     A person pushes it. Nothing waits on that push -- the carry reads the checkout's working
     files, so the revision is carryable the moment it is committed -- but until it happens the
     revision has had no CI run and its `source_commit` names a commit only this machine holds.
     Measured precedent: change record 62's intake registered against 10b13d47, a revision this
     producer committed to local `main` on 2026-08-19, and the lane completed end to end.

     A SECOND PASS OVER AN UNCHANGED QUEUE WRITES NOTHING. The producer advances a package only
     when it does not already carry the bump in an approved revision; otherwise it replays, and
     change-manager answers 200 for an identical proposal keyed on the package revision.

     SCOPE IS THE AUTHORED SET, not a list in this file. A repository is in this lane because
     somebody authored a standing package targeting it, so widening the lane is an authoring act
     in intent-packages and never an edit here.

     RunAtLoad is false. A missed firing needs no catch-up: the next pass reads the same open
     pull requests and proposes whatever is still unproposed.

     THE EXIT CODE IS THE REPORT, AND 0 DOES NOT MEAN THE PASS DID NOTHING. launchd discards
     it, so read the log -- 0 nothing arose that needs a person for an anomalous reason, WHICH
     INCLUDES a pass that revised a package, committed it and proposed a record; 1 the tool
     failed on a credential; 2 it ran but could not use its inputs (no standing packages, a
     dirty checkout); 3 a finding -- an untranscribed gate, a title and trailer that disagree, a
     stranded record, a refused proposal. `proposed` is deliberately not a finding: it is this
     job's ordinary output, and the person it needs is the one who approves the record in
     change-manager rather than the one who reads this log. Read the lines, not the code, to
     learn whether anything was written.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.devon.bump-proposer</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>__REPO_ROOT__/scripts/run-bump-proposer.sh</string>
        <string>--submit</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>6</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>50</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- Homebrew is on this list because `gh` and `bws` live there, and the wrapper needs
             both: `bws` for the propose-scoped change-manager bearer, `gh` for the GitHub token
             it has no BWS record for. -->
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>__HOME__</string>
        <!-- The checkout this pass revises and commits into. The wrapper defaults to the same
             path; it is stated here because it IS the answer to where the pass writes, and the
             carry at 07:05 reads this same working copy. -->
        <key>BUMP_PROPOSER_PACKAGES_CHECKOUT</key>
        <string>__HOME__/Projects/intent-packages</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/bump-proposer.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/bump-proposer.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
